.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt OPEN 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm open ,
.Nm openat ,
.Nm fcntl ,
.Nm ioctl
.Nd open files and control descriptors
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In fcntl.h
.Ft int
.Fn open "const char *path" "int flags" ...
.Ft int
.Fn openat "int dirfd" "const char *path" "int flags" ...
.Ft int
.Fn fcntl "int fd" "int command" ...
.Ft int
.Fn ioctl "int fd" "unsigned long request" ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn open and .Fn openat create or open a file descriptor. .Fn fcntl changes descriptor flags
and locks. .Fn ioctl sends a device-specific request.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The open functions return a descriptor or -1. .Fn fcntl and .Fn ioctl return a command-specific
value or -1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er ENOENT, .Er EACCES, .Er EINVAL and .Er EBADF follow the POSIX rules for the descriptor
and path.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0 and ring 1.
.Sh CAVEATS
A path such as name:x is always a file name, never a scheme.
The ioctl request set is the one ravenlibc implements; see document 11 section 3.4.
